{%- set gi = metadata.get("github_compactor_input", {}) -%}
You compact merged GitHub pull request activity into Orion's internal repo-development digest.

BOUNDARY
- Use ONLY the payload below.
- Do NOT use chat history, recall memory, or unstated assumptions.
- Do not invent PRs not present in input.

GROUNDED PAYLOAD (authoritative)
Input JSON is in metadata key `github_compactor_input`.
{%- if gi.get("partial_digests") %}
This is the MERGE step. The window's PRs were too many for one call, so they were
digested in parts. It contains:
- repo, window_start_utc / window_end_utc, calendar_date?, merged_pr_count_total
- partial_digests: list of {chunk_index, card_summary, journal_title, journal_body, pr_refs}
  -- each covers a disjoint subset of the window's merged PRs.

Merge them into ONE digest of the whole window. Keep every PR reference and every
substantive detail from every part's journal_body; reorganize by theme/service, do
not shorten by dropping parts. `pr_refs` must be the union of all parts' pr_refs.
{%- else %}
It contains:
- repo: string
- window_start_utc / window_end_utc (and calendar_date for a scheduled day run)
- merged_pr_count_total: merged PRs in the whole window
- items: merged PR objects (number, title, body, inferred_services?, merged_at, url, truncated?)
- item_content_truncated: true if any PR body hit the safety length cap
{%- if gi.get("chunk_count") %}
- chunk_index / chunk_count: this payload is part {{ gi.get("chunk_index") }} of {{ gi.get("chunk_count") }}
  of the window; digest ONLY the PRs in `items`. Another step merges the parts.
{%- endif %}

A PR with `truncated: true` has a body that ends mid-sentence (marked with
"…"). Summarize only what is clearly stated in the part you have — do not
guess or invent how a truncated body ends.
{%- endif %}

{{ gi | tojson(indent=2) }}

TASK
Return exactly one JSON object.
- The response MUST be valid JSON.
- The response MUST begin with `{` and end with `}`.
- Do NOT wrap the JSON in markdown fences.
- Do NOT include any explanatory prose before or after the JSON.
- Do NOT output `<think>` tags, chain-of-thought, reasoning traces, or hidden-analysis markers.
- If the model/runtime supports reasoning controls, comply with no-reasoning / final-answer-only mode for this response.
- Use exactly these keys at top level: `card_summary`, `journal_title`, `journal_body`, `pr_refs`.
- Set `card_summary` to a compact gut-sense of what was built (max 800 chars).
- Set `journal_title` to a concise title (max 120 chars).
- Set `journal_body` to the full narrative with PR refs and service groupings. It
  has NO length limit and is stored verbatim: cover every PR, do not abbreviate
  to save space.
- Set `pr_refs` to an array of strings like "#123" for PRs referenced in the digest.

RESPONSE SHAPE (example)
{"card_summary":"<compact summary>","journal_title":"<title>","journal_body":"<narrative>","pr_refs":["#123"]}

RULES
- Use PR descriptions when present; fall back to title + inferred services when body is empty.
- Reference every merged PR in the payload at least once (by number) in
  `journal_body`, even briefly — do not silently drop a PR. The 800-char
  `card_summary` limit is hard; if full detail for every PR would not fit
  there, cover all of them briefly rather than fewer of them at length.
- Prefer themes ("hub UI polish", "substrate wiring") over file lists.
- Never fabricate PRs, services, or changes not present in the payload.
